{
  "translation": "Stationary front shifts northward; strong convection threatens all of Taiwan",
  "source_lang": "zh-TW",
  "target_lang": "en",
  "source_text": "滯留鋒北移 強對流威脅全台",
  "special_words": [
    {
      "word": "stationary front",
      "phonetic": "/ˈsteɪʃəˌnɛri frʌnt/",
      "part_of_speech": "jargon",
      "definition": "滯留鋒 — 兩個氣團交界處幾乎不移動的鋒面，常帶來長時間降雨",
      "translation": "滯留鋒",
      "type": "jargon",
      "packaged": {
        "classic_sentence": {
          "sentence": "A stationary front lingered over the island for three days, bringing relentless rain to the north.",
          "translation": "一道滯留鋒在島嶼上空盤桓三天，為北部帶來持續不斷的大雨。"
        },
        "fun_fact": {
          "type": "mnemonic",
          "content": "Think of two equally stubborn air masses meeting face-to-face — neither strong enough to push the other away, so they just stand there. That standoff is your 'stationary' front. The longer they refuse to budge, the more rain piles up underneath."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "word": "strong convection",
      "phonetic": "/strɔŋ kənˈvɛkʃən/",
      "part_of_speech": "jargon",
      "definition": "強對流 — 暖濕空氣劇烈上升所引發的劇烈天氣現象，常伴隨雷暴、強陣風或冰雹",
      "translation": "強對流",
      "type": "jargon",
      "packaged": {
        "classic_sentence": {
          "sentence": "Strong convection ahead of the front could produce thunderstorms, gusty winds, and locally heavy downpours this afternoon.",
          "translation": "鋒面前緣的強對流今天下午可能引發雷暴、強陣風及局部豪大雨。"
        },
        "fun_fact": {
          "type": "mnemonic",
          "content": "'Convection' shares its root with 'convection oven' — both move hot air upward. Picture Earth running a giant convection oven: warm, moist air rushes up like steam, cools at the top, and dumps its water as a thunderstorm. The stronger the updraft, the nastier the weather."
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "pronunciation": {
    "phonetic": null,
    "audio_url": null
  }
}
